# Line-ending policy for Chicago-Ventra-Mars-Cubic-Analysis
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Contributors work on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so text files were
# checked out CRLF. That is harmless until a file is copied from the Windows
# worktree into a Linux context -- which is exactly what `docker build` does.
# dashboard/docker-entrypoint.sh reached the image as "#!/bin/sh\r", naming an
# interpreter that does not exist on Linux, so the nginx entrypoint hook failed
# silently: /config.js was never rewritten, the bundle fell back to the baked
# VITE_API_BASE_URL, and /healthz still returned 200 because it is a static
# nginx response. A wrong API base behind a green health check.
#
# Every .sh in this repo had the same latent defect (29 of them, including all
# the Lambda deploy.sh scripts). They worked only because CloudShell clones get
# LF. Declaring the policy here removes the dependency on each contributor's
# local git config.

# Default: git decides what is text, and text is LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything executed by a POSIX shell or copied into a Linux image must be LF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts stay CRLF.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.xls       binary
*.docx      binary
*.pptx      binary
*.parquet   binary
*.joblib    binary
*.pkl       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary

# Notebooks are JSON: keep them LF so diffs and nbformat round-trips are stable.
*.ipynb     text eol=lf
